  "notes": "SOURCE: https://www.cartwheelsgymcentre.com/programs.php\nCartwheels Gym Centre - Programs About Programs Adapted Programs Registration Events Parties Contacts Cartwheels Programs Program Registration Schedule at a glance Tiny Gym (1 and walking to 3 years) 45 minutes $140.00 per term --> Your child's first gym class! This class is for our youngest gymnasts with their parent/caregiver. It focuses on both sensory and gross motor development, co-ordination, balance, strength, flexibility, social skills, and fun!! **The 1-year old participants are strongly recommended to be fully independently walking before the term begins. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY 9:15 - 10:00 10:15 - 11:00 TUESDAY 9:15-10:00 10:15 - 11:00 4:00 - 4:45 5:00 - 5:45 6:00 - 6:45 WEDNESDAY 10:15 - 11:00 5:00 - 5:45 6:00 - 6:45 THURSDAY not scheduled SATURDAY 9:30 - 10:15 10:30 - 11:15 SUNDAY 8:30 - 9:15 9:30 - 10:15 10:30 - 11:15 --> Rock n' Roll with Miss Kelly (0+ years) 45 minutes $140.00 per term --> This class offers a safe environment for your child to grow physically, cognitively, and socially through music and movement. In this class we will use sensory rich props and musical instruments as we enjoy interactive playtime through song, dance, and physical literacy. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. Music Instructor - Platinum Music Instruction - Gold Tumble & Learn (2y 11m to 4 years) 2 hours $ per term --> Preschool & Kindergarten readiness program at Cartwheels. Tumble n’ Learn will focus on gross and fine motor development; sensory skills; strength, coordination, balance, and flexibility; independence and social skills. This two-hour drop-off program will include 45-minutes of a structured gymnastics class, music class, learning activity, group games, and a healthy snack break (nut/peanut free snack brought weekly by participants). This program allows participants to register for longer than one term length for increased development and continuity for the children Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. Mini Gym (3/3½ - 4 years) 45 minutes $140.00 per term --> Our eligibility rule for Mini Gym is that they have just participated in our Tiny Gym program (in the term prior to their move to Mini Gym) AND are showing signs of readiness to participate without a parent, OR are already 3 ½ when registering. If your child is new to Cartwheels, OR is a returning member with a break between participating in our terms, and they are not yet three years + six months prior to the term start date, they must register into Tiny Gym. This is to learn the routine, expectations, and structure of our program. No exceptions due to the demand & limited Mini Gym spots. **Participants must also be fully toilet trained (no pull-ups) to register into Mini Gym. If you choose to proceed with registration past the pop-up informing you of these requirements, you will be contacted to move to Tiny Gym or refund/credit your registration until they are eligible. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY 9:15 - 10:00 10:15 - 11:00 5:15 - 6:00 TUESDAY 9:15 - 10:00 10:15 - 11:00 4:00 - 4:45 WEDNESDAY 9:15 - 10:00 5:00 - 5:45 6:00 - 6:45 THURSDAY not scheduled SATURDAY 8:30 - 9:15 9:30 - 10:15 11:30 - 12:15 SUNDAY 10:30 - 11:15 --> Kindergym (4-6 years) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> A fast paced class geared to channel this age group's energy in a positive direction. This class provides opportunities to build social skills, self-confidence, and develop physical and motor attributes including: flexibility, strength, power, and endurance as well as balance and spatial orientation. All this in a gymnastics setting! Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY 4:00 - 4:50 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 WEDNESDAY 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 THURSDAY 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 SATURDAY 8:30 - 9:20 9:30 - 10:20 10:30 - 11:20 11:30 - 12:20 SUNDAY 8:30 - 9:20 9:30 - 10:20 11:30 - 12:20 --> JR Gym (6-8 years) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> This recreational program is for those wanting to experience the fun and thrill of gymnastics! The program promotes physical fitness and allows children to achieve new skills by focusing on their strengths and encouraging development of their weaker areas. They work on an achievement program consisting of a system of progressive skills that each child works on at their own pace. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY 5:00 - 5:50 WEDNESDAY 4:00 - 4:50 7:00 - 7:50 THURSDAY 5:00 - 5:50 6:00 - 6:50 SATURDAY 10:30 - 11:20 11:30 - 12:20 SUNDAY 11:30 - 12:20 --> SR Gym (8-10 years) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> This recreational program is for those wanting to experience the fun and thrill of gymnastics! The program promotes physical fitness and allows children to achieve new skills by focusing on their strengths and encouraging development of their weaker areas. They work on an achievement program consisting of a system of progressive skills that each child works on at their own pace. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY 6:30 - 7:20 TUESDAY 7:00 - 7:50 WEDNESDAY 4:00 - 4:50 7:00-7:50 THURSDAY 5:00 - 5:50 7:00 - 7:50 SATURDAY 11:30 - 12:20 SUNDAY not scheduled --> Preteen/Teen Gym (ages 10+) 60 minutes $154.00 per term --> This recreational program is for those over age 10 wanting to experience the fun and thrill of gymnastics! The program promotes physical fitness and allows children to achieve new skills by focusing on their strengths and encouraging development of their weaker areas. They work on an achievement program consisting of a system of progressive skills that each child works on at their own pace. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY not scheduled WEDNESDAY not scheduled THURSDAY 7:00 - 7:50 SATURDAY not scheduled SUNDAY not scheduled --> Cartwheels Plus Programming (5 years to teen) 55 minutes $154.00 per term --> An invitation only advanced class open to those that need to be challenged at a higher level and can handle being taught at a faster rate than our other programming. This class will focus on strength and flexibility training as well as more advanced skills. Participants must be invited from Cartwheels programming and registration requires a code to unlock the program. Availability and pricing available by logging into our Registration Website. Pricing information is not available on the main site due to the terms varying in length over the season, resulting in pricing fluctuations term by term. MONDAY not scheduled TUESDAY not scheduled WEDNESDAY not scheduled THURSDAY 6:00 - 6:50 SATURDAY not scheduled SUNDAY not scheduled --> Ability Athletics Special Needs Programming - Social Sports - Playability - Movability Program Information Cartwheels Gym Centre &copy; Website by Nakoda Creative\n\nSOURCE: https://www.cartwheelsgymcentre.com/\nCartwheels Gym Centre - Home About Programs Adapted Programs Registration Events Parties Contacts Gymnastic Programs We offer fun and exciting recreational gymnastics classes with our certified qualified coaches. Adapted Programs Inclusive adaptive programming for neurodivergent individuals with special needs, offering 1:1 support. Camps School may be out, but we are just getting warmed up. Cartwheels offers full-day or half day camp options, taking place on select school breaks. Gym Parties A welcoming and exciting place to host your special event. You bring the cake - we take if from there! Welcome to Cartwheels -- Participant Information Memo Welcome to our gym! Cartwheels offer recreational gymnastic instruction in a fun filled, energetic environment. Located in Georgetown Ontario, in a clean professional facility, our qualified coaches are excited to teach your little gymnast! Read more Georgetown’s favourite recreational gymnastics centre News from the gym... Our events Weekly Recreational Gymnastics Classes Music Programming for Littles Special Needs Programming School Break Camps Party Bookings for members of Cartwheels Important News: Stay in the loop: The best way to stay in the loop on all things Cartwheels, is to follow us on social media. You'll find us both on Facebook and Instagram. Not on social media? You can find our most recent Facebook posts in the \"News from the gym\" highlight box here on our website. Facility Expansion: In December 2022, we renovated our 6400 sq/ft facility to a 12,800 sq/ft facility to better meet the needs of our community and add much-needed programs for children with special needs. Cartwheels Awarded Readers' Choice Diamond Best Kids Activities 2022 Diamond Best Gymnastics Club 2021 Platinum Best Family Activities Best Kids Activities Best Kids Camps Best Recreation Facility Best Summer Camps Watch our social media to stay in the know with all things going on at Cartwheels! --> Registration Information: Program Registration: Term 1/Fall registration is Wednesday July 22, 2026 - 8:00am online for all general programming and Tumble n' Learn* - 10:00am by email request for Ability Athletics programs, Playability* and Moveability* *programs registered for an extended period that includes the dates of Term 1 and Term 2. Our Programs Register On-Line Visit our Registration page for information about our discount offers! Contacts Cartwheels Gym Centre 12 Armstrong Ave. Georgetown, ON L7G 4R9 +1 905 702 9904 Email: info@cartwheelsgymcentre.com Cartwheels Gym Centre &copy; Website by Nakoda Creative\n\nSOURCE: https://www.cartwheelsgymcentre.com/forms/Term_2_Schedule_2026-27.pdf\n%PDF-1.6 %���� 734 0 obj > endobj 758 0 obj >/Filter/FlateDecode/ID[ ]/Index[734 37]/Info 733 0 R/Length 115/Prev 176754/Root 735 0 R/Size 771/Type/XRef/W[1 3 1]>>stream h�bbd`\u0010``b``� \"\u0019W��r ��\u001e�d�\u0001\"����W0y\u0012L����`5���\u0017�H�(\u0010Y�\u0011l�% ��=\u001b�� \"���~�HMM���`��`�\u0001��\u001f������)\u0017$\u0002\u0014#������ �\u0000(;\u0015[ endstream endobj startxref 0 %%EOF 770 0 obj >stream h�b``\u0010c``��\u0000$�5\u0019P\u0001#\u0010�0p4 ��A1\u0003�\u0001�\u0000�;�u�\u001d��\u0019�2�d��x�y\u001fs1�Vq#â�l��\u001e�\u0019N��d�f e`�� f$S�V���@�205�\u0006�\u001c ��pKx\u0018�6:CT1�\u0003\u0004\u0018\u0000��\u0017� endstream endobj 735 0 obj >/Metadata 10 0 R/Outlines 14 0 R/PageLayout/SinglePage/Pages 732 0 R/StructTreeRoot 17 0 R/Type/Catalog>> endobj 736 0 obj >/ExtGState >/Font >/Pattern >/XObject >>>/Rotate 0/StructParents 0/Tabs/S/Type/Page>> endobj 737 0 obj >stream h޴�mO\u001b1 ��J>nB,�΋4Mj;�����nc 